    {
      "title": "Two's Complement and Negative Numbers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Two's Complement and Negative Numbers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Encoding",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rule: ==-x = ~x + 1== (flip all bits, add 1)",
                "Top bit has weight ==-2^(n-1)==, the rest are positive",
                "8 bits: `1111 1111` = -128 + 127 = **-1**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Range and Hardware",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Signed n-bit range: ==-2^(n-1)== to ==2^(n-1) - 1==",
                "8 bits: -128 to 127, so one more negative than positive",
                "{red:abs(INT_MIN)} overflows: +2^(n-1) does not fit",
                "Signed and unsigned share the ==same adder== for + and -"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Lowest Bit and Gotchas",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==x & -x== isolates the lowest set bit",
                "-x flips every bit above it and keeps it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Python ints are unbounded: negatives need `& 0xFFFFFFFF`",
                "Left-shifting a signed int into the sign bit is undefined in C/C++"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "print(-1 & 0xFFFFFFFF)",
                "print(12 & -12)"
              ],
              "note": "32-bit view of -1; lowest set bit of 12"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "4294967295",
                "4"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why two's complement?** One adder serves signed and unsigned.",
                "**abs(INT_MIN)?** Overflows, there is no +2^(n-1).",
                "**What is x & -x?** The lowest set bit."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check, Set, Clear, Toggle and x & (x-1)",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check, Set, Clear, Toggle and x & (x-1)",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bit i Operations",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Op",
                "Expression"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Check",
                  "`(x >> i) & 1`"
                ],
                [
                  "Check (mask)",
                  "`(x & (1 << i)) != 0`"
                ],
                [
                  "Set",
                  "`x | (1 << i)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Clear",
                  "`x & ~(1 << i)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Toggle",
                  "`x ^ (1 << i)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. x & (x-1)",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "x",
                    "sub": "10100",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "x-1",
                    "sub": "10011",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "x & (x-1)",
                    "sub": "10000",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`x-1` flips the ==lowest 1== and every 0 below it",
                "So `x & (x-1)` ==clears the lowest set bit==",
                "Power of two: `x > 0 && (x & (x-1)) == 0`",
                "A power of two has ==exactly one== set bit"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`x & 1 == 0` parses as `x & (1 == 0)`; write `(x & 1) == 0`",
                "`1 << i` overflows int for i >= 31; use `1L << i`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Parenthesize",
              "text": "`==` and `!=` bind tighter than `&` in C, C++, Java: wrap the masked part."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "XOR Tricks, Counting Bits and Bitmask Subsets",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "XOR Tricks, Counting Bits and Bitmask Subsets",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. XOR Tricks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Single number: ==XOR all== elements, pairs cancel",
                "Lone value left: O(n) time, O(1) space",
                "`1^2^1^3^2^5` = `3^5` = `011^101` = `110` = 6",
                "Two unpaired values: XOR is their ==combination==, not either one",
                "Swap: `a ^= b; b ^= a; a ^= b`",
                "{red:Breaks} if both names are one variable"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Counting Bits",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Kernighan: `x &= x - 1` runs once per ==set bit==",
                "Builtins: `popcount`, `bit_count()`, `Integer.bitCount`",
                "DP for 0..n: `bits[i] = bits[i >> 1] + (i & 1)`",
                "Or `bits[i & (i-1)] + 1`, O(n)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "while x:",
                "    x &= x - 1",
                "    count += 1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Subsets by Bitmask",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Loop mask from 0 to `(1 << n) - 1`",
                "Include item i when `mask & (1 << i)`",
                "==2^n== subsets, fine for n up to ~20"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "for mask in range(1 << n):",
                "    pick = [a[i] for i in range(n)",
                "            if mask & (1 << i)]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Pairs cancel; `x &= x - 1` drops one bit per step."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
