              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What does `x & (x-1)` return for x = 12, and what is it doing?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "x = 12 (`1100`), x-1 = 11 (`1011`), so the result is 8 (`1000`)",
                "It clears the lowest set bit"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What is the XOR of [1,2,1,3,2,5], and what does it mean?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "6 = 3 ^ 5, since 1s and 2s cancel in pairs",
                "It is the XOR of the two unpaired values, so it cannot return either one alone"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "In 8-bit two's complement, what is `1111 1111`, and why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "-1: the top bit weighs -128 and the other bits add 127",
                "Check: ~1 + 1 = `1111 1110` + 1 = `1111 1111`"
